== Notes ==

*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
*Most NWN manuals state that [[weapon focus]] is a prerequisite, but it is not. 
* This feat [[stack]]s with any [[massive critical]] item property on a weapon (including that obtained from [[thundering rage]]).
* The number of extra dice rolled does not match the feat's description.
** There is an additional 1d6 rolled &ndash; this feat adds +2d6 for a x2 multiplier, +3d6 for x3, and +4d6 for x4.
** Only 1d6 is rolled if [[ki damage]] is used for an attack, regardless of the critical multiplier. This results in less average damage for a critical hit (by 1 for a x2 multiplier, more for higher multipliers). So a [[weapon master]] could average more damage by not using ki damage in situations where critical hits are frequent enough (based on the [[threat range]]).
* The [[creature weapon]] variant of this feat is non-functional; the [[unarmed strike]] variant is used with creature weapons (or any other [[natural weapon]]).
*Weapons with the [[no combat damage]] property do not benefit from overwhelming critical.

=== Previous versions ===

* Prior to [[Enhanced Edition]] version 1.89,<!--might have been fixed earlier--> this feat did not account for a weapon master's ''[[increased multiplier]]'' feat; a [[kukri]] (normally a x2 weapon) would still get a +2d6 bonus from this feat, even when it has a x3 multiplier in the hand of a weapon master.